  "question": {
    "text": "The radius of a calcium ion is $94 \\mathrm{pm}$ and of the oxide ion is $146 \\mathrm{pm}$. The possible crystal structure of calcium oxide will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PEWxQ",
      "text": "\ntetrahedral\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "z6cvQ",
      "text": "\ntrigonal\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MkL2s",
      "text": "\noctahedral\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ArpjK",
      "text": "\npyramidal",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As per formula,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text { radius ratio } & =\\frac{\\text { radius of cation }}{\\text { radius of anion }} \\\\\n& =\\frac{94}{146}=0.643\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSince the value is between $0.414-0.732$ hence the coordination no. will be 6 and geometry will be octahedral.",
    "image": null
  },
